The minimum number of wins is $\lceil \frac{20}{11}\rceil=\lceil 1\frac{9}{11}\rceil=2$, which, in this problem, can only be achieved for the student who loses all $20$ games. This student has the minimum average wins of $\frac{2n}{n}=2$, and the best possible average wins is $\frac{11\cdot 10}{11}=10$, so the answer is $\boxed{2\text{ and }10}$. </think> <answer> 2\text{ and }10 </answer>

